 of information by the axon: 1. Noise and memory in the myelinated nerve fiber of the frog</article-title><source>Biol Cybern</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>67</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">172162</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030079-b032"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Coleman</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahns</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Rowe</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Impulse propagation over tactile and kinaesthetic sensory axons to central target neurones of the cuneate nucleus in cat</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>550</volume><fpage>553</fpage><lpage>556</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12766249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030079-b033"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fox</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Stochastic versions of the Hodgkin&#x02013;Huxley equations</article-title><source>Biophysical J</source><volume>72</volume><fpage>2068</fpage><lpage>2074</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030079-b034"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jack</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Noble</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsien</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>1983</year><source>Electric current flow in excitable cells. 2nd edition</source><publisher-loc>Oxford</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Oxford University Press</publisher-name><page-count count="518"/></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030079-b035"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Swadlow</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Waxman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>1975</year><article-title>Observations on impulse conduction along central axons</article-title><source>Proc Nat Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>72</volume><fpage>5156</fpage><lpage>5159</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030079-b036"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Debanne</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Guerineau</surname><given-names>NC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gahwiler</surname><given-names>BH</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Action-potential propagation gated by an axonal Ia-like K&#x0002b; conductance in hippocampus</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>389</volume><fpage>286</fpage><lpage>289</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9305843</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030079-b037"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cecchi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Sigman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Alonso</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Chialvo</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Noise in neurons is message dependent</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>97</volume><fpage>5557</fpage><lpage>5561</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10792057</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030079-b038"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Waxman</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Bennett</surname><given-names>MV</given-names></name></person-group><year>1972</year><article-title>Relative conduction v